From: reverb-g2-linux lab <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 04:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] nvkms: do not clamp to 6 bpc when the EDID leaves color
 depth undefined

An EDID 1.4 digital sink may leave the "Color Bit Depth" field of the Video Input
Definition byte (0x14, bits 6-4) set to 000 = "undefined". nvt_edid.c parses that
into `input.u.digital.bpc = 0`:

    default :
        pInfo->input.u.digital.bpc = 0;
        break;

nvDpyGetOutputColorFormatInfo() then tests `bpc < 8` for DisplayPort sinks, which
is true for that 0, and clamps the display to 6 bpc:

    } else if (...digital.bpc < 8) {
        colorFormatsInfo.rgb444.maxBpc = ..._BPC_6;
        colorFormatsInfo.yuv444.maxBpc = ..._BPC_UNKNOWN;

Since ChooseColorBpc() returns `max` when nothing specific was requested, such a
sink ends up driven at 6 bpc (18 bpp) for every mode.

"Undefined" means the sink did not declare a depth, not that it wants 6. The DSI
branch of this very function already treats the unknown case as 8:

    default:
        nvAssert(!"Unsupported bpc for DSI");
        // fall through
    case 8:
        colorFormatsInfo.rgb444.maxBpc = ..._BPC_8;

so DP and DSI disagree on the same input today. Windows drives the same sinks at
8 bpc.

Found on an HP Reverb G2 (EDID 1.4, ManufID 0x220E, byte 0x14 = 0x80, and a
DisplayID 2.0 extension that carries no Display Parameters block, so nothing
overrides the parsed 0). Measured on the wire:

  nvidia-modeset: DPCONN> Notify Attach Begin (Head 0, pclk 428580000
                          raster 2980 x 1598  18 bpp)

and the headset's own status report says 6 bits per component on Linux against 8
on Windows with the same GPU. Its 90 Hz modes do not light the panel at 6 bpc;
its 60 Hz mode does.

Treat 0 as "not declared" and let it fall through to the 8 bpc default.
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-dpy.c
@@ -3453,7 +3453,8 @@
                     colorFormatsInfo.rgb444.maxBpc =
                         NV_KMS_DPY_ATTRIBUTE_CURRENT_COLOR_BPC_10;
                     colorFormatsInfo.yuv444.maxBpc =
                         NV_KMS_DPY_ATTRIBUTE_CURRENT_COLOR_BPC_10;
-                } else if (pDpyEvo->parsedEdid.info.input.u.digital.bpc < 8) {
+                } else if (pDpyEvo->parsedEdid.info.input.u.digital.bpc != 0 &&
+                           pDpyEvo->parsedEdid.info.input.u.digital.bpc < 8) {
                     colorFormatsInfo.rgb444.maxBpc =
                         NV_KMS_DPY_ATTRIBUTE_CURRENT_COLOR_BPC_6;
                     colorFormatsInfo.yuv444.maxBpc =
